// parity-expected-stdout-begin
// 1
// "hi"
// parity-expected-stdout-end

// Generalize-by-arity, unconstrained half — roadmap G5, shipped in 0.0.7.
//
// `identity` carries no annotation at all. It takes a parameter and raises no
// class constraint, so it is given a scheme and each call site instantiates it
// fresh. Before G5 the first call pinned the parameter and the second was a
// type error.
//
// The boundary is the constraint, not the annotation: `fn double(x) { x + x }`
// raises `Num` and is still monomorphic. See
// ../../failing/compile/b2_unannotated_constrained_double.flx.

fn identity(x) { x }

fn main() with IO {
    print(identity(1))
    print(identity("hi"))
}
